entry='''

## Part 450 — 2026-10-23 — Simultaneous/alive handoff and fatal peer restart

**Part status:** scoped local acceptance completed; exact publication-head full CI/packages are tracked in PR.
**Objective and scope:** observe both lexical pending collisions, alive false/bad-cookie/valid handoff and actual owned peer-tree termination/restart against pinned OTP29.1.1, with full raw protocol/error/frame and physical cleanup evidence.

### Changes and decisions

- Merge449 PR10 only after exact35fa2383 CI is green; main7e4a324d merge CI39951441544 passes8825/8825, all mandatory steps and both package builds. No NuGet release.
- Build final Runtime6B102A98 and fresh actual native package863E7814 before protocol runs. Reuse BCL/ETF/process/native infrastructure and own Halt437 Toolhelp layout; no new dependency, production net_kernel rewrite or runtime algorithm change. Original Erlang/BEAM libraries remain unchanged. Read exact pinned Git blobs rather than newer checkout HEAD.
- Hold an actual original outgoing NAME before status, then initiate a competing connection to that original VM. Original net_kernel genuinely emits nok for its higher lexical name and ok_simultaneous for the lower one; the selected direction adopts the actual pre-created runtime pending handle, loser stays unadopted. Check both orders, not guessed simulated states.
- Alive false and true with wrong cookie preserve the existing physical data stream and runtime generation. Valid true verifies cookie before original wait_pending; actual old socket closes, host controller joins before host ACK read/new adoption. Same peer creation/new generation and actual original sys_dist ctrlr/conn_id replacement are retained. Do not claim wire ACK arrival time or unrecorded post-negative original row equality.
- Capture the actual owned original process family with retained handles/start times, force its tree to terminate, join all captured processes, observe nodedown/absence and restart the same node name with new PID/creation. Python creator requires designated nonzero exit plus matching operation receipt; unexpected cleanup forcing still fails. Legacy ForcedTermination receipt field denotes cleanup fallback only; ExpectedScenarioTermination and fatal family receipts identify the actual planned kill. This is not Job containment or a fabricated unload after VM death.
- Surviving local DDLL refs/queue1 and old external wire identity survive handoff/fatal peer death. Same-VM memory survives alive replacement; actual peer memory is lost on OS death. Fresh replacement monitor queue1 rejects old peer refs and is canceled only by its fresh ref to0. Full badarg/error/frame profiles0/1/2/8 remain compared unchanged.
- Add one permanent managed candidate/queue/epoch HOST group: duplicate adopter refusal and AbortPending on a connected generation preserve the whole live snapshot/output; actual queued data delivers; releasing old lease/controller after reconnect leaves the new controller alive. Constants live in a separate type file. HOST controls are distinct from actual original network observations.

### Validation and next boundary

- First immutable observer packet passes both depth8 orders, then all remaining0/1/2 orders without repeating depth8:400/400 observations =352 paired source/protocol +48 auxiliary guards;344 whole typed/raw +56 explicit own-reference rows. Both batches use identical final runtime, observer and BEAM. No failed scenario, relaxed expected value or forced product fix.
- Independent audit recomputes24 successful cookie reply/ACK pairs,8 wrong-cookie and8 false-alive refusals,2695 inputs per batch and6427 original-provider files before/after. Eight designated nonzero original exits match16 captured joined family handles;16 oracle/replacement VMs and two private EPMDs exit normally. All24 authenticated channels drain to0 and join; native children/leases clean up.
-589/589 affected in30 immutable blocks, retained36/DDLL native8, standard79 and actual collector/persistent cleanup pass. New canonical group passes; catalog8825→8826. Default708/full118/source guards1621 stay unchanged, API/full deltas0/0. Style/readiness and exact publication-head full CI/packages are explicit publication gates; historical8813 readiness authority is not relabelled current full8826.
- Preparation efficiency: one observer packet/two successful nonoverlapping batches, versus449's five failed preparation/observer runs and later final-binary rebind. Final binaries are built first to avoid that repeat. Cold85.672s versus warm~1–2s provider scans reflect caching, not algorithm speedup. CI attempts and durations are recorded separately in PR.
- [Full immutable proof](../validation/part-450/ddll-simultaneous-alive-and-fatal-peer/README.md). Current status/module milestones/remaining-work docs updated. Remaining: check_pending/already_pending, broader simultaneous/setup/handoff races, malformed/legacy/dynamic negotiation, TLS/full managed standard net_kernel boot/autoconnect/priority ALTACT, wider DDLL/native/platform contracts. No whole-module or performance promotion. Keep LICENSE.local.txt excluded.
'''
